{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CeDmjhw6wUEKdaWdwqDU4","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All post-check gates pass, no model resident, 106 GiB free. Iteration 2 is complete.\n\n## Ladder item 1.2 — single-CTA radix select for the indexer top-k\n\n**Shipped.** `include/topk_radix.h`: MSB-first 8-bit radix select over a 64-bit composite key `comp(v,t) = (ord(v) << 32) | ~t`, one gather, one bitonic sort of the ≤512 winners. All four kernels take it (`k_topk_verify`, `k_topk_decode`, `k_topk_masked`, `k_topk_offset`). `DSV4_TOPK_RADIX=0` restores the warp scan and is the A/B arm.\n\nBecause `~t` makes every composite distinct there are no ties to break, so the select needs no equal-key case. Two details are load-bearing: admission stays the original's **float** compare `v > floorv` (a key-space test would select NaN, which the original cannot), and `-0.0` is folded onto `+0.0` before the key is formed (`index_score` can emit `-0.0`; the raw bits order them differently than the original's `>` does).\n\n**Measured — paired, same corpus, baseline arm first, 35/52 legs paired exactly on tau and width:**\n\n| ctx | before | after | paired Δ | band | speedup | tau b/a | tok/s |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 12,410 | 167.18 | 154.66 | **−12.55** | [−12.92, −12.33] | **1.081×** | 1.652/1.652 | 9.88 → 10.69 (**+8.2 %**) |\n| 9,341 | 166.77 | 156.54 | −10.47 | [−10.66, −10.15] | 1.065× | 1.969/1.969 | +6.7 % |\n| 6,260 | 154.62 | 146.23 | −8.58 | [−8.65, −8.30] | 1.057× | 1.718/1.718 | +5.8 % |\n| 3,197 | 147.85 | 141.23 | −6.72 | [−7.01, −6.28] | 1.047× | 1.626/1.626 | +4.8 % |\n| 1,664 | 140.91 | 136.41 | −4.53 | [−5.07, −4.40] | 1.033× | 1.701/1.701 | +3.3 % |\n| 889 | 132.80 | 130.30 | −2.34 | [−2.84, −2.18] | 1.019× | 1.724/1.724 | +1.9 % |\n\n`b`: 3.488 → 2.514 ms/1000; paired saving `3.122 + 0.793 ± 0.031 × ctx/1000`, R² 0.951. That is **91 % of the 0.872 ± 0.021 that 0.4 attributed to `i:topk`, and the 2 SE band [0.730, 0.856] does not cover it** — the 9 % is recorded, not rounded away.\n\nThe **3.12 ms context-independent** part is the finding: `i:topk` marks only `k_topk_verify`; `k_topk_decode` on the draft side has never had a dprof mark. Same blind spot that hid `draft:main_kv` — the profile is still incomplete, for the second time.\n\n**Bit-exactness.** Unit gate on 4 shapes × 13 lengths × 6 distributions (exact ties, signed zeros, floor-straddling, all-negative) PASS, clean under memcheck; in-situ `DSV4_TOPK_GATE=1` memcmp of the whole index array against the untouched warp kernel — **11,008 calls, 183,179,703 slots, 0 FAIL**; standing GATE and LOSSLESS gate PASS at tau 2.87.\n\n**Killed in the same iteration:** `__match_any_sync` warp-aggregated histogram is slower (43.0 vs 39.0 µs at T=3072) despite the contention diagnosis being right — written to `negative-results.md`.\n\n**A trap, recorded:** Phase 4 first ran zero seconds after the previous server exited, was refused for lack of memory before the page cache was reclaimed, and the script printed \"decode finished; gates:\" followed by nothing and exited 0 — a missing gate looking exactly like a passing one. Fixed (wait on `MemAvailable`, assert the log is non-empty and carries the PASS line) and written to `measurement-and-traps.md` §14.\n\nWiki updated in the same change: `kernel-optimisations.md` §2.6, `context-scaling.md`, `negative-results.md` §4b, `measurement-and-traps.md` §14, `README.md` state table.\n\n**Not committed by me** — `.claude/settings.json` denies `git add/commit/push` to the agent. The prepared message is at `evidence/decode_loop/COMMIT_MSG_1p2.txt` and `scripts/decode_loop.sh` (pid 7591, running) commits and pushes with it on the iteration's behalf, which is the sanctioned path."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":699,"cache_read_input_tokens":244367,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_