     before    after    paired d   band                speedup   tau b/a        tok/s\n  12,410   167.18    154.66   -12.55     [-12.92, -12.33]    1.081x    1.652/1.652    9.88 -> 10.69 (+8.2 %)\n   9,341   166.77    156.54   -10.47     [-10.66, -10.15]    1.065x    1.969/1.969   11.81 -> 12.60 (+6.7 %)\n   6,260   154.62    146.23    -8.58     [ -8.65,  -8.30]    1.057x    1.718/1.718   11.12 -> 11.77 (+5.8 %)\n   3,197   147.85    141.23    -6.72     [ -7.01,  -6.28]    1.047x    1.626/1.626   10.93 -> 11.46 (+4.8 %)\n   1,664   140.91    136.41    -4.53     [ -5.07,  -4.40]    1.033x    1.701/1.701   12.08 -> 12.48 (+3.3 %)\n     889   132.80    130.30    -2.34     [ -2.84,  -2.18]    1.019x    1.724/1.724   12.95 -> 13.19 (+1.9 %)\n\n  before   fwd = 130.60 + 3.488 x (ctx/1000)     after   fwd = 129.11 + 2.514 x (ctx/1000)\n  paired   saving = 3.122 + 0.793 +/- 0.031 x (ctx/1000)      R^2 0.951, n=35\n\nWHAT IT MEANS. The context term is down another 28 %, and 65 % cumulatively from the 7.220 the\nladder opened on. 0.4's dprof attributed 0.872 +/- 0.021 ms/1000 to `i:topk`; the paired measurement\nrecovered 0.793 +/- 0.031, whose 2 SE band [0.730, 0.856] does NOT cover the prediction. 9 % short,\nrecorded rather than rounded away.\n\nThe interesting number is the other one. The saving also has a 3.12 ms/forward CONTEXT-INDEPENDENT\ncomponent, which no profile in this repo could have predicted: `i:topk` marks `k_topk_verify` and\nnothing else, and `k_topk_decode` — the identical kernel on the draft side — has never had a dprof\nmark at all. That is the same blind spot that hid `draft:main_kv` until 0.4 went looking. A win that\nlands in the intercept says the profile is still incomplete, for the second time.\n\nTerm A is now much the larger problem: 129.11 ms of a 154.66 ms forward at ctx 12,410 (83 %), and\n1.57x its 82.18 ms byte floor. Neither stop condition is met; the loop continues.\n\nWHAT SHIPPED. include/topk_radix.h: MSB-first 8-bit radix select over a 64-bit composite key\ncomp(v,t) = (ord(v) << 32) | ~t, one gather, one bitonic sort of the <= 512 winners. All four\nkernels take it (k_topk_verify, k_topk_decode, k_topk_masked, k_topk_offset). O(T) work in a\nconstant number of passes instead of `topk` SEQUENTIAL argmax rounds -- 14-34x standalone, 18.0x at\nT=3072 (ctx 12,288). DSV4_TOPK_RADIX=0 restores the warp scan exactly.\n\nBecause ~t makes every composite distinct there are no ties to break, so the select needs no\nequal-key special case. Two details are load-bearing and each has its own gate distribution:\nadmission is the original's FLOAT compare v > floorv and never a key-space test (ord(NaN) beats\nevery finite key, but NaN > best is false); and -0.0 is folded onto +0.0 before the key is formed\n(-0.0f == +0.0f is a tie for the original, but ord(-0.0) < ord(+0.0) as raw bits, and index_score\ncan emit -0.0).\n\nBIT-EXACTNESS. Order is load-bearing, not just the set: sparse_attn sums the selected rows in order,\nso a reordering changes fp32 association.\n  tests/gate_topk_radix.cu   4 kernel shapes x 13 lengths x 6 distributions   PASS\n    (exact ties, signed zeros, floor-straddling rows, all-negative)\n  ^ under compute-sanitizer --tool memcheck                                   0 errors\n  dsv4-server in situ, DSV4_TOPK_GATE=1: 11,008 calls, ctx to 12,282,\n    183,179,703 index slots, prefill + extend + rewind                        0 FAIL\n  standing GATE + LOSSLESS gate (build/decode)                                PASS, tau 2.87\nThe in-situ gate launches the UNTOUCHED warp kernel with identical arguments into a private buffer\nand memcmps the entire index array, aborting on the first differing slot -- the substitute hard\ninvariant 1 names after 1.0's amendment, since token ids are not a valid test at context.\n\nBUILT AND KILLED IN THE SAME ITERATION (wiki/negative-results.md 4b): a __match_any_sync\nwarp-aggregated histogram is SLOWER (43.0 vs 39.0 us at T=3072, 57.5 vs 49.3 at T=8192) even though\nthe contention diagnosis behind it was right. Block size was worth sweeping: 128/256/512/1024 =\n53.3/38.9/32.0/31.6 us at T=3072; 512 shipped.\n\nA TRAP, RECORDED (wiki/measurement-and-traps.md 14): PHASE 4 first ran 0 seconds after the previous\nserver exited, was refused by run_model.sh for lack of memory (page cache not yet reclaimed), and\nthe script printed \"decode finished; gates:\" followed by nothing and exited 0. A missing gate looked\nexactly like a passing one. Now it waits for MemAvailable and asserts the log is non-empty and\ncarries the PASS line.\n\nWIKI, in the same commit: kernel-optimisations.md 2.6 (adopted win), context-scaling.md (the term),\nnegative-results.md 4b (the two dead levers), measurement-and-traps.md 14 (the trap), README.md\nstate table.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nEOF\ngit add -A\ngit commit -F evidence/decode_loop/COMMIT_MSG_1p2.txt -q && git log --oneline -1","description":"Commit"}},{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_0126qtQqxeHHMToC6K44RC4d","tool_input":{"command":"git add -A && git status --short | wc -l","description":"Stage all changes"}},{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_01UWyCjYHN5hhUaS7GYKxgWu","tool_input":{"command":"git add -A","description":"Stage all changes"}},{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_0178zhzZEDYXJGfp5Tq8PHB9","tool_input":{"command":"git add DECODE_LADDER.md include/topk_radix.h kernels/compressed_decode.cu kernels/indexer.cu tests/gate_topk_radix.cu scripts/topk_ab_run.sh scripts/build_gate.sh scripts/decode_loop.sh scripts/decode_loop_watchdog.sh scripts/detach_audit.sh wiki/README.md wiki/context-scaling.md wiki/kernel-optimisations.md wiki/measurement-and-traps.md wiki/negative-results.md evidence/","description":"Stage the change set by path"}}],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"All post-check gates pass, no