{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01EN335jXY561rrLmBfbY5kK","type":"tool_result","content":"92:# AN ITEM THAT CANNOT BE FINISHED MUST NOT BE RE-SELECTED FOREVER. next_item takes the topmost\n93:# unchecked entry, and the prompt tells the agent to leave an item it cannot complete UNCHECKED\n94:# rather than fake progress. Those two rules together are a livelock: the next iteration picks the\n103:# PRIORITY IS DATA, NOT TEXT ORDER. \"Topmost unchecked\" hard-codes the order the ladder was written\n133:                  '- [!] **' + iid + '**  _(DEFERRED by the loop: ' + why + '. Reopen by hand -- change `[!]` back to `[ ]`.)_\\n     ', 1)\n148:Do EXACTLY ONE ladder item this iteration — the topmost unchecked one — then stop.\n187:in the ladder entry and leave it unchecked rather than faking progress.\n199:  [ -n \"$item\" ] || { say \"no unchecked ladder items left\"; break; }\n237:This is iteration $iter. The topmost unchecked ladder item is:\n246:    say \"ITERATION TIMED OUT after ${ITER_TIMEOUT}s (rc=$rc) — leaving the ladder item unchecked\"\n336:  # ATTEMPT BOOKKEEPING. If the topmost unchecked item is STILL the one this iteration was given,\n343:      say \"item $ITEM_ID still unchecked after this iteration (attempt $n/$MAX_ATTEMPTS)\"\n349:The loop takes the topmost unchecked item and the prompt tells it to leave an item it cannot finish\n350:unchecked. Together those re-select the same item forever. Deferring keeps it visible in the ladder","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f3675501-4e06-40a6-a91c-c3ec4ba4cfd0","uuid":"0945ceed-397b-4e77-adc6-e735ceb3bbf6","timestamp":"2026-08-20T14:53:12.608Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"92:# AN ITEM THAT CANNOT BE FINISHED MUST NOT BE RE-SELECTED FOREVER. next_item takes the topmost\n93:# unchecked entry, and the prompt tells the agent to leave an item it cannot complete UNCHECKED\n94:# rather than fake progress. Those two rules together are a livelock: the next iteration picks the\n103:# PRIORITY IS DATA, NOT TEXT ORDER. \"Topmost unchecked\" hard-codes the order the ladder was written\n133:                  '- [!] **' + iid + '**  _(DEFERRED by the loop: ' + why + '. Reopen by hand -- change `[!]` back to `[ ]`.)_\\n     ', 1)\n148:Do EXACTLY ONE ladder item this iteration — the topmost unchecked one — then stop.\n187:in the ladder entry and leave it unchecked rather than faking progress.\n199:  [ -n \"$item\" ] || { say \"no unchecked ladder items left\"; break; }\n237:This is iteration $iter. The topmost unchecked ladder item is:\n246:    say \"ITERATION TIMED OUT after ${ITER_TIMEOUT}s (rc=$rc) — leaving the ladder item unchecked\"\n336:  # ATTEMPT BOOKKEEPING. If the topmost unchecked item is STILL the one this iteration was given,\n343:      say \"item $ITEM_ID still unchecked after this iteration (attempt $n/$MAX_ATTEMPTS)\"\n349:The loop takes the topmost unchecked item and the prompt tells it to leave an item it cannot finish\n350:unchecked. Together those re-select the same item forever. Deferring keeps it visible in the ladder","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
