{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VKWUs3hPS2kEHvSZP8ub4a","type":"tool_result","content":"14:## 1. The transformations that generalised\n20:### 1.1 \"Read B once\" — amortise a weight read across every row that uses it\n43:### 1.2 Thread-per-output is wrong at decode shapes\n56:### 1.3 Stage more per barrier\n67:## 2. Structural wins\n69:### 2.1 Full-step CUDA graph (F44)\n78:### 2.2 The arena (F44, F83)\n93:### 2.3 Adaptive verify width (F49, F59, F63)\n102:### 2.4 Fork/join the kv chain (F57)\n107:### 2.5 Don't recompute a prefix that cannot have changed — cache the main-KV (ladder 1.0, 2026-08-20)\n206:### 2.6 A selection sort is not a top-k — single-CTA radix select (ladder 1.2, 2026-08-20)\n317:### 2.7 Change which kernel the bit-exactness claim is *against* — `index_score` as a register-tiled GEMM (ladder 1.5, 2026-08-20)\n389:### 2.8 The one adopted win that is not a kernel — actually serve the head you trained (ladder 2.2, 2026-08-20)\n418:## 3. Precision and layout\n432:## 4. What every adopted change has in common\n=== traps sections ===\n116:## 11. Gate the shape range the engine spans\n125:## 12. The engine stops reproducing itself part-way through a long run, so \"bit-identical token ids\" is not a test there\n179:## 13. A gate that passed, reported as a failure, because the probe it rode on kept no records\n200:## 14. A phase that ran nothing, and reported \"finished\"\n239:## 15. Put a leg the change *cannot* touch inside the same sweep\n278:## 16. A fitted slope is only \"cost per 1000 context\" if the mark is linear in context\n313:## 17. A launch that failed, and a `cudaStreamSynchronize` that called it success\n393:## 18. The device opt-in maximum is not the kernel's maximum, and the safety margin that failed a passing gate\n428:## 19. The variance is BETWEEN checkpoint loads, not within them — 0.6 % vs 5.7 %\n471:## 20. A gate that does not compile is a gate that passes by never running (ladder 1.5, 2026-0